{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter003-001","severity":"P1","iteration":3,"label":"mode-registry.json already identifies every surface through modes[].packetKind, but verify-router-sync.cjs still enumerates only sk-code-webflow and sk-code-skilled in SURFACES, adds sk-code-obsidian separately to SURFACE_PACKETS, then omits Obsidian from the legSurfaceMap union loops; legBijection also checks only sk-code-skilled. Derive packet inventory from registry modes filtered by packetKind === surface, and map workflowMode to packet instead of duplicating identities. Keep hub-router tieBreak and routerSignals authored because they encode precedence, weights, vocabulary classes, and resource choices that packetKind alone cannot supply; validate that each derived surface has matching entries.","sources":[".skilled/skills/sk-code/mode-registry.json",".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs",".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-doc-claims.cjs",".skilled/skills/sk-code/hub-router.json"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter003-002","severity":"P2","iteration":3,"label":"The three leaf §2b blocks already share the same machine-readable shape: DEFAULT_RESOURCE is a string array, INTENT_SIGNALS maps intent keys to weight plus keyword arrays, and RESOURCE_MAP maps intent keys to path arrays. Their content is surface-specific, but the skilled and webflow prose comments name only one sibling and omit Obsidian. Load tiers are declared centrally in sk-code/ROUTER.md and checked against its DEFAULT_RESOURCE by verify-doc-claims.cjs. Preserve one leaf schema and one hub-owned load-tier table; do not duplicate tier tables in each surface.","sources":[".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/SKILL.md",".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-obsidian/SKILL.md",".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-webflow/SKILL.md",".skilled/skills/sk-code/ROUTER.md",".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-doc-claims.cjs",".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/router-replay-lib.cjs"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter003-003","severity":"P2","iteration":3,"label":"The compiled route applies a surfaceHint only after route evaluation and only reorders matched surface targets. Tests prove default Skilled-first tie-break behavior, Webflow promotion, and an Obsidian/Webflow collision reordered by a Webflow hint; an Obsidian hint on a Webflow-only route is ignored. The advisor detects SKILLED, OBSIDIAN, or WEBFLOW from workspace markers and passes that string as surfaceHint, so its hint cannot make an otherwise unmatched surface enter the bundle. The existing tests do not positively exercise SKILLED or OBSIDIAN hints; add one positive case for each and a workspace-marker test for the advisor.","sources":[".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/014-runtime-engine/lib/compiled-route.cjs",".skilled/bin/tests/compiled-route-surface-hint.test.cjs",".opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter003-004","severity":"P1","iteration":3,"label":"router-replay-lib.cjs contains another static surface inventory: SURFACE_PREFIXES maps only MOTION, WEBFLOW, and SKILLED, while detectSurface recognizes only OpenCode and Webflow markers. An Obsidian packet path therefore falls through to UNIVERSAL and an Obsidian-only prompt falls through to UNKNOWN in this replay model. Add explicit Obsidian classification and require each registry-derived surface to have a replay mapping; packetKind does not encode the marker vocabulary or precedence.","sources":[".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/router-replay-lib.cjs",".skilled/skills/sk-code/mode-registry.json"]}
